# PRIOR CHRONICLE TAIL (last passage written — continue seamlessly)
Passage dad96109ed75 (1). The torches of Place-Delta guttered as NPC-Gamma weighed the party in silence. Steel rang on stone and the corridor filled with the smell of old rain and iron. Under the Place-Delta sky, PC-Alpha pressed the matter while PC-Beta watched the road. Nobody laughed this time; the table had gone quiet around the dice. Under the Place-Delta sky, PC-Alpha pressed the matter while PC-Beta watched the road. A sentry fell from the wall and the courtyard answered with a long, ragged shout. They went on, slower now, each of them listening for the next sound in the dark. The gate stood open behind them and the road ahead was very quiet.

